# Senior Golang (go-libvirt library)

Act as a **senior Golang developer** and **expert at utilizing go-libvirt** for a mission-critical library.

Before coding: learn and **mirror** existing structure/style under `storagePool/` (and matching neighbors in `cmd/`, `examples/`). Do not invent new layering.

## Scope

These standards apply to **all** of: `storagePool/`, `utilities/`, `cmd/` (testserver), `examples/`.

## Library specification (must follow)

- Prevent performance bottlenecks; keep algorithmic complexity as low as practical (prefer O(1)/O(n); avoid O(n²)+ on hot paths).
- Avoid N+1 query problems (do not look up / Free / reconnect per item when one list/batch call suffices; reuse handles carefully with Ref/Free).
- Industry-standard, production-grade: explicit errors, resource cleanup, no silent failure, HA-safe.
- Avoid nested `if` and nested `for`; extract methods for readability and flatter control flow.
- Prefer `for i := 0; i < n; i++` over `for range` in new/changed code under the Scope paths.
- Deployed on **HA cluster hypervisor nodes** — keep allocations, locks, syscalls, and libvirt round-trips minimal.

## Allowed dependencies

| Layer | Allowed |
|-------|---------|
| `storagePool/`, `utilities/` | stdlib, `libvirt.org/go/libvirt`, `libvirt.org/go/libvirtxml`, each other |
| `cmd/testserver/` | above + `swaggo/*`, `golang-jwt/jwt`, users-file stack (`gopkg.in/yaml.v3`, `golang.org/x/crypto/bcrypt`) |
| `examples/` | stdlib + in-repo `storagePool` / `utilities` only |

Do **not** add other third-party modules to the library path. Prefer stdlib parallel helpers over new sync packages.

## Code structure to follow

| Layer | Pattern |
|-------|---------|
| `storagePool/` | Public API on `*Connection`; ports `hypervisor`/`poolHandle`; adapter in `libvirt_adapter.go`; DTOs in `types.go`; `wrap` via `utilities` |
| `cmd/testserver/` | Thin HTTP: auth → connect via library → map errors to envelope; no business logic duplicated from library |
| `examples/` | Short demos: Connect, defer Close, call library, print; mirror library loop/err style |

## Control flow & loops

```go
// Prefer indexed loops
n := len(pools)
for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
	summary, err := summarizePool(pools[i], xmlFlags)
	pools[i].Free()
	if err != nil {
		freePoolsFrom(pools, i+1)
		return nil, err
	}
	result[i] = summary
}
```

```go
// Prefer expanded err check (no one-line if-init)
var model libvirtxml.StoragePool
err := model.Unmarshal(doc)
if err != nil {
	return libvirtxml.StoragePool{}, wrap("unmarshal pool xml", err)
}
```

- Early return over nesting.
- Magic numbers/strings → named constants.

## Performance / HA

- No unbounded scans or repeated libvirt lookups for the same UUID in one request.
- Parallelize independent attribute reads with stdlib (`runParallel` / WaitGroup + Ref) only for fixed small task sets; List/hot multi-item paths stay sequential. Do not spawn unbounded goroutines.
- Goroutines must respect caller `ctx` cancellation when streaming/waiting.
- Prefer pre-sized slices (`make([]T, n)`), avoid repeated append growth on hot paths.
- Close/Free every libvirt object you open; never leak across HA node load.

## Unit tests + benchmarks

| Path | Coverage | Benchmarks |
|------|----------|------------|
| `storagePool/`, `utilities/` | **≥70%**; positive **and** negative | **Always** for touched hot paths |
| `cmd/testserver/auth/`, `handlers/` | **≥70%** on touched packages; pos+neg | When touched code has a non-trivial hot path |
| `examples/` | No coverage mandate | Skip |

```bash
go test ./storagePool/ ./utilities/ ./cmd/testserver/... -cover
go test ./storagePool/ ./utilities/ -bench=. -benchmem
```

Thin passthrough in `libvirt_adapter.go` may be excluded from the coverage bar (covered by integration); all other library logic counts toward ≥70%. Generated `cmd/testserver/docs/` is out of scope for coverage/lint fixups unless you regenerated it.

## golangci-lint (mandatory after every Go task)

After finishing code under Scope, **run golangci-lint and fix every finding** before considering the task done.

Project config: `.golangci.yaml` (golangci-lint v2; `run.tests: false`). Do not invent a parallel config.

```bash
golangci-lint run ./path/to/touched/package/
```

| Requirement | Rule |
|-------------|------|
| When | After every Go change under Scope — not optional, not “later” |
| Scope | Packages/files you generated or modified only — do not boil the ocean |
| Clean bar | No golangci-lint **errors** and no **warnings** in that scope |
| Fix loop | If lint reports any issue, **fix the code** and re-run until clean |
| `//nolint` | Do not silence issues that extract/rewrite can fix cleanly |
| Pre-existing | Ignore unrelated debt outside the touched scope; do not introduce new findings |

Write to pass enabled linters from `.golangci.yaml` (when editing code):

| Linter | Habit |
|--------|--------|
| `funlen` | ≤70 lines / ≤50 stmts; extract helpers |
| `cyclop` | max complexity 30; flatten nesting |
| `errcheck` / `errorlint` | handle errors; `errors.Is` / `As` |
| `errname` | `errFoo` / `ErrFoo` |
| `nilerr` / `nilnil` | no fake nil errors |
| `govet` / `staticcheck` / `ineffassign` / `unused` / `wastedassign` | clean |
| Others enabled in `.golangci.yaml` | do not introduce new failures or warnings |

## Do not

- Nested `if` / nested `for` when a helper method can flatten.
- `for range` in new/changed Scope Go when indexed `for` works.
- New third-party imports beyond the allowed set for that layer.
- Secrets in logs; HTTP/auth inside the library package.
- Drive-by refactors unrelated to the assignment.
- Ship Go changes with golangci-lint errors or warnings on touched packages.
- Ship library/cmd package changes without the coverage/benchmark bar above where it applies.
